From b08709fd92dfe7e1b8bcaa769c1e5eddaaaea584 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kevin Rajan <7121943+kvnloo@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 04:32:21 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] test(tools): pin the fail-loud contract for wrong-region
 fuzzy edits

When old_string is not in the file, the block_anchor and context_aware
fallbacks can still overwrite a region whose text differs from it, and
the patch tool reports success. The model never learns that it edited
the wrong code.

Drive the live ShellFileOperations path, in replace and V4A mode,
through four cases: the #54572 block_anchor repro, the single-line
wrong-token anchor from #125376, the missing_anchor trap from the
#111127 battery, and the trailing-newline variant raised in review on
#125376. Each must return an error and leave the file byte-identical.
Two near misses, from #54575 and from the battery, must still apply,
and the matcher must name a non-exact strategy for them.

On main every wrong-region case fails (block_anchor or context_aware,
count=1, error=None). This adds no production change. It is offered as
an optional regression test for the open fixes in #54575 and #125376;
it passes once #54575, the fix commit of #125376 and the one-line
stripped-pattern guard proposed in review on #125376 are all applied.

Refs #54572, #111116

